WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.520
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.650
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.990
Rola.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.750
I'm back, Yume.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.500
Welcome back, Rola.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.510
Rola.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.770
Rola, you look like a weight's been lifted from your shoulders.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.520
I finally found the answer I was looking for.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.190
Have you? That's great.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:52.990
Thanks.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.700
What about you?

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.410
I...

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.280
I've still gotta find my own answer!

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.660
Let's switch to the next outfit.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.040
Mahiru-chan, eyes on the camera.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.290
There!

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.550
Let's touch up your makeup.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.760
Her growth has been simply outstanding.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.800
Certainly.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.340
In fact, I have a proposal for her.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.180
<b>Kasumi Mahiru-chan New Serial Feature Plan</b>

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.180
My own regular feature?

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.730
Haven't you been asking for one?

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:29.110
Yes, but only popular models get regular columns.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.440
Mahiru, you're more than popular enough as a model.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.450
I'm... a popular model? {did they really have to repeat it three times? I'm considering 'established' but because they're just repeating each other...}

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.280
Yes, you are.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.820
I'm expecting great things.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.080
Right!

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.050
Sakuraba-san's amazing!

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:25.140
She landed a job the instant she came back!

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:30.020
<i>Rola's completely different than before. She's incomparably better!</i>

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.980
Yume, listen to this!

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.650
What's going on?

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:39.740
Mahiru just got a regular feature in Aikatsu Style Girls!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.320
A regular feature?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.910
So what do you plan on writing about?

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:49.580
Well, my sister does the Kasumi Yozora Advice Corner and such.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.870
Oh?

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.580
What about you, Mahiru?

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.460
I'm not Kasumi Yozora.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.340
I want to have a column that's uniquely mine.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.340
What would that be like?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.630
I'm not sure.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.840
If we look at that which is unique to Mahiru...

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.930
Tick tick tick tick...

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:06.850
Ding-dong!

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.850
After a full search through my mental database,

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:14.350
your ideal column is the Perfectionist's Meticulous Lesson!

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.270
What kind of lesson would that be?

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:17.610
Its contents...

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.320
are for you to consider.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.360
Oh no!

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.200
I forgot that I had an extra interview scheduled today.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.120
Huh?

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:30.620
Mahiru and I must also be off to our 
Aikatsu Style Girls appointments.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.120
Both of you?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.790
Yes, mine is for a fashion page. {this use of page seems fine, but who knows what you've edited up until now}{I assume it's separate from the other thing though}

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.000
I'm taking an interview about my recent part in a movie.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.750
We'll see you after.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.010
S-Sure.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:45.840
<i>Everyone is incredible. I need to work harder so I don't get left behind.</i>

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:51.270
It feels somewhat strange to be heading to the studio together.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.020
True, but it's a welcome change of pace.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:01.150
Goodness, who's littering?{I think you made ako go full neibs-descriptor-ess this episode}

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.280
What...

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.790
What a magnificent tissue this is!

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.370
Wouldn't you agree, Mahiru?

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.750
You dropped this.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.130
What's she on about?

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.760
Legit cray.{for crazy, it's short for hanpanai. the long form shows up later}

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.420
Mahiru, let's move on!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:30.510
The streets aren't your trash can, and sitting there will just get in the way of others. {it's a convenience store}

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.810
Talk about a downer. You mad?

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.140
We're in high school.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.690
Sure you should take that attitude with your seniors?

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.320
It's pretty cray.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.320
F-F-Forgive us kindly!

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.190
Mahiru!

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.820
There's a trash can behind you.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:48.910
Why, you!

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:05.010
Ah, right. Don't we have a mountain of homework today?

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.470
Cray, right?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.970
Run away!

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.390
For goodness' sake.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:18.350
Why must you always be such a goody two-shoes?

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.310
I couldn't just sit there and do nothing.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.610
A segment unique to me...

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:29.990
Hello!

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.370
Do you have a minute?

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.780
Rola?

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:36.120
Look, a souvenir.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.830
I made some for everyone, but forgot to hand them out.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.790
Hot springs sour konbu...

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:44.750
It's sour konbu we made at the hot springs! Try one!

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:50.890
Sour!

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.680
Good, isn't it? Eat up and re-energize.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:55.260
Bye.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.640
Oh, Rola!

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:01.900
Don't you think that Yume's been acting a bit strange?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.690
A lot's happened to her.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:09.030
Koharu leaving must have been a huge shock in itself,

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.570
but then she couldn't finish that song for her.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.370
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.410
But Yume said she'd work hard.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.670
She's trying to pull herself back up.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:25.920
So there's only one thing we need to do.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.920
Watch over her, right?

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.930
I'm sure she'll be fine.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:34.300
Of course. Yume's my rival.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.060
<i>But deep inside,</i>

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:40.270
<i>Rola must desperately want to see Yume.</i>

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:05.880
Mahiru! B-B-Big trouble!

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.670
Mahiru! Mahiru!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.090
There you are!

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.380
What's going on this early?

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.880
R-R-R-Revenge!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.930
What?

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.510
What do you need from Mahiru?

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.520
Such a downer. You mad too?

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.520
What's going on?

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.520
Oh yeah, you mad.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.480
Look! They're here for revenge, as I thought!

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.570
Rola.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:31.900
This is all because of what you did!

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.490
I'm right here.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.660
Mahiru.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.160
Kasumi Mahiru, right?

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.290
Do you have business with me?

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:46.540
I heard you took care of my girls yesterday.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.040
And so?

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.550
Come with me for a bit.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.050
Fine.

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.770
A chocolate muffin and chocolate cookies!

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:12.940
A chocolate drink and chocolate ice cream!

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.530
Let's see, there's also...

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:17.950
Hold on!

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.700
Actually, why are you doing this?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.620
Don't you like chocolate?

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.870
I mean, I do.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.620
I-Is it not enough?

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.540
You two, go buy up all the chocolate!

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.920
Aye!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:33.050
That's not what I meant. What are you doing?

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.760
Making up for troubling you the other day.{that was getting somewhat apologetic apostrophe-y}{dude, the makup segmetn didn't even start yet}

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.390
Sumiko-san is a fan of yours.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.510
Huh?

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:43.390
It's not Sumiko, it's Susan! 
We picked them just the other day!

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.770
You're Monica, from Motoko,

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:48.270
and you're Amy, from Eiko.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.230
Um...

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:51.190
Yes?

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.530
Thank you for your support.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:10:00.280
Th-Think nothing of it! As your number one fan, 
I've studied far and wide to perfect my impression.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.660
Impression? Of me?

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.290
Yes! Just look at me.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:09.170
I'm using you as a reference for my hairstyle, makeup, and fashion.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.960
Uh, you're way off the mark.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.260
That's exactly the problem.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.630
I can't tell what I got wrong.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.380
Should I've gone more all out?

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.720
You wanted to add more?

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.890
It's no good?

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:25.430
Makeup is all about the balance between accentuating and reducing.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.520
Don't just keep adding to the parts you want to emphasize.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.270
Instead, you should soften the other areas in order to bring them out.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:36.690
Um, if it's all right with you, would you mind teaching us your techniques?

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.570
What?

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:40.700
We wanna shine like you do, Mahiru-san!

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.280
Not like this, but more bright and shiny!

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.540
Come on, you two beg her too!

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:46.950
Please help us!

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:52.500
I understand. In return, 
you'll listen to everything I say.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.460
Are we clear?

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:54.880
You'll really do it?

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.090
Thank you!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.640
Doesn't it seem like they're getting along?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.550
Utterly impossible!

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:08.100
They must have stuffed that 
ordinary-looking muffin with wasabi!

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:09.980
They're coming this way!

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:13.730
Hey! Return Mahiru at once!

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.480
Ako, it's okay.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.610
What is okay?

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:24.370
Thanks for worrying about me, but I'm just fine.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.660
A-Are you now?

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.250
Thank you too, Rola.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.370
Sure.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.120
Let's go, girls.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.210
Okay!

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:33.630
I'm so excited!

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.040
You can count on me.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.420
I guess she really is fine.

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:39.840
So it appears.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.140
Legit cray!

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:47.140
There aren't any shoots today, 
so I got permission to use this room.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.640
For real?

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.520
Then let's begin.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.980
It's Mahiru's Stylish Girl Lesson!{I wonder if it's okay to use Stylish for always instead of like, Fashion}

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.150
First, you'll need to remove your makeup.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:57.440
What?!

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:58.230
Cray!

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.820
Didn't you promise to do everything I said?

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.070
B-But...

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:05.820
Do you want this or not?

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:08.160
We'll do it!

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:21.220
That's what I thought. You weren't tan, you just used a dark foundation.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.930
Now for the styling lesson.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.850
But really, you all have such unique hairstyles.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.640
I wanted to have wavy hair like yours, Mahiru-san. {I wonder if there's not a word for wavy in japanese}{the answer to every question like this is no}

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:34.690
My hair is thin, so I wanted to thicken it.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.610
Cray.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:41.150
I see. Then let's start with...

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.450
You, Susan.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.860
You can make your hair wavy with a curling iron.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.870
There, now that looks nice. {that looks like my brush there}{be careful, someone might doxx you}

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:54.790
Then let's treat Monica's cuticles.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.750
Amy gets a bandana.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:02.590
Then we use wax to rein in her straggly hair, and we're done!

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.510
Next, stylish makeup techniques.{if this is a thing with the Stylish Girl Lesson thing it should a thing like this}{I almost guarantee it won't be, but i'll leave a batch note just in case}

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:09.510
Oh, this is what we usually use.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:13.520
No, reduction makeup suits you the best, Monica.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:18.060
You have large eyes, so use eyeliner on about one-third of your lower eyelids. {two men with no makeup experience arguing in subs about makeup}

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:21.020
And your eyelashes are long, so you don't need fake ones.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:26.490
We'll stick with brown mascara, 
and try to aim for a natural finish.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.530
Amy, your cheeks have a faint natural pink.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.540
We won't use any blush on your cheeks,

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:36.080
instead applying it beneath your eyes.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:41.040
We call this complexion makeup, 
and it gives your face a healthy sheen.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.720
Susan, would you prefer red or pink lipstick?

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:46.800
There's only one choice for me...

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.680
White lipstick!

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:51.140
I think red would look great on you.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.560
This red is a little strong,

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:57.640
but if we touch it up with a translucent gloss...

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.610
This is us?

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:03.280
For real?

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.940
Cray!

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:07.240
You all have lovely smiles.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:10.240
And while we're at it, let's be more careful with our words as well. {I was going to use something like 'speak more politely/less crass', but ended up gravitating to this}{I thought of a good alternative, and then I forgot what it was}

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.280
Okay!

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:14.870
All right, you two—I mean, ladies,

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.330
let's clean up!

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.960
Yeah!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.580
But honestly, everyone looks so much nicer. {have to check this}

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.290
Changing their makeup seems to have cleared their hearts as well.{lengthish}

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.590
Yeah, you're seriously cute!

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:23.710
Yeah, yeah!

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.260
Wonderful.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:27.670
Editor.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:32.970
Orchestrating such a cute transformation shows your fierce talent.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:36.680
All I did was apply makeup that I thought would look nice.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:39.140
Not everyone can do what you did.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:43.230
You feel a duty to help those in need.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.900
That's your individuality!

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:48.740
My individuality...

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:52.490
I've got it! Let's make this your regular feature.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:55.990
We'll call it Mahiru's Stylish Girl Lesson!

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:58.000
Okay!

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:03.500
And since we're on the topic, why don't we announce it at next week's fashion show? {}{maybe collaboration needs to be stuck into it}

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.380
Are you sure?

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.010
But that means...

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.510
You three.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:09.510
Yes?

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.890
I'll have you model in my fashion show!

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.140
Let's get started with your model lessons!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.140
The key to modeling is posture!

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:24.150
Walking is all about balance! {???}{assuming it's 重視度 definitely ???}

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.150
Good, keep looking straight.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:29.570
Mahiru-san!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.990
We can't do this after all.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.030
This is crazy... {or we could go further}{crazy is just short for crazy-craze after all...}

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.660
What comes after two? {oh my god}

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.290
Three? {it works! thank the gods}{you are solely to blame}

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.370
Yep! Those are beautiful smiles.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:44.540
The most important thing to remember up on stage is to smile.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:49.460
It's okay if you mess up. All you need to do is embrace the stage.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.050
Smile...

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.050
What comes after two?

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.550
Three!

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.270
<i>Good, now one last thing.</i>

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.060
Yume.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.570
Mahiru-chan, what's up?

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:11.820
I have something for you.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.240
A ticket?

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:16.070
You'll run out of steam if you work too hard.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.830
You need to take a breather sometimes.

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:20.910
Thanks, Mahiru-chan!

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.960
Yume, over here!

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:27.880
Rola! Ako-chan!

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.420
You're late.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:32.510
Sorry, I lost track of time doing Aikatsu.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.930
For you, Yume.

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:35.970
Sour konbu?

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:40.470
Sour!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.890
But there's a hint of sweetness.

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:50.360
Thank you for your patience. Aikatsu Style Girls presents...

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:52.740
The Stylish Girl Collection.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:56.620
I will be your host,

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.490
Kasumi Yozora.

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.330
It's beginning!

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:04.000
This gets me going!

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:07.000
It feels like my heart is in my throat!

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.000
This is crazy!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:14.510
Don't worry. You were brave enough to do your makeup on the sidewalk and show up at Four Star Academy.

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:15.630
But...

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.260
What comes after two?

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.760
Three!

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:25.640
Starting us off will be guests of the new feature, Kasumi Mahiru's Stylish Girl Lesson,

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:28.650
Monica & Amy.{what's your take on using & for アンド?}

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:39.620
They're totally different!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.660
I can hardly believe my eyes!

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.290
Following them is Susan.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:03.350
She's so cute!

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.230
Mahiru, you're a frightful one.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:11.110
And finally, the architect behind their 
transformations and a popular idol herself,

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:12.520
Kasumi Mahiru.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.610
Everyone, thank you for coming.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.110
Mahiru!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:19.610
Mahiru-chan!

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:23.490
Next, Kasumi Mahiru will hold a performance.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:31.630
Studded with rhinestones, the Brilliant Freeze Coord.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:36.380
Kasumi Mahiru, like a radiant light!

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:47.070
I can't wait to see what kind of top model she'll mature into.

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:54.580
Mahiru!

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.790
Today's fashion show was fabulous!

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:59.040
Congratulations.

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.840
Thank you very much.

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:02.210
Mahiru-neesan!

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:03.260
"Nee-san"?

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:06.170
We owe this all to you, Mahiru-neesan!

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:10.390
You're so cool and mature and fashionable.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:13.270
It's like... you saved us!

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:14.720
We'll follow you forever!

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:16.480
And that's not crazy!{uh... oh, fine}

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:24.230
Mahiru-neesan... it's a bit embarrassing, but it's got a nice ring to it.

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:12.800
What should I do if that power takes over again?

00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:15.220
Yume-chan, strengthen your heart!

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:18.430
But I'm scared of taking the stage!

00:24:18.430 --> 00:24:20.640
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.640 --> 00:24:22.190
The Chosen Stars.

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.480
Become the first-star idol!
